\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Project: Production-Ready Cross-Platform rPPG Vital Signs App\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1. Your role\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Act as a principal Flutter engineer, mobile computer-vision engineer, machine-learning deployment engineer, UX designer, QA engineer, and application security engineer.\
Build a complete, production-quality Flutter application for Android, iOS, and web that demonstrates open-source remote photoplethysmography (rPPG) for estimating physiological signals from a live camera feed.\
The product should be inspired by the general user experience of iSelfie-style contactless health measurement apps, but must have its own original branding, interface, code, and assets. Do not copy proprietary assets, source code, or distinctive copyrighted designs.\
This is a real implementation project, not a mockup, tutorial, or architecture-only exercise.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Your primary responsibility is to create a working, testable application with a real signal-processing pipeline, a documented model integration, secure data handling, automated tests, and release-build preparation.
\f1\b0 \
Do not stop after generating a plan. Inspect the repository, implement the application, run available checks, fix failures, and document anything that remains blocked.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2. Product vision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Build a polished contactless physiological-sensing application that allows a user to:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Understand the technology and its limitations.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Grant camera permission and position their face in a guided frame.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Complete a camera-based measurement session.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 View a heart-rate estimate when the signal passes quality checks.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Inspect a pulse waveform and measurement-quality indicators.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Optionally view respiratory-rate estimates if the selected algorithm supports them adequately.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Review previous measurements and trends.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Export or delete their measurement history.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Learn about the underlying open-source algorithms, their licenses, and their limitations.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
